// cg_saxpybuf — fused vector update y = sc[cy_slot]·y + sc[cx_slot]·x, with the two
// coefficients read from the GPU SCALAR BUFFER (not a push constant), so no CPU
// round-trip. x = set 2, y = set 3 (in place). Slot 6 holds 1.0 and slot 7 holds 0.0
// for the "constant" coefficients (copy / axpy).
//
// DIMENSION-GENERIC (solver-ledger.md §7d). This file used to carry its own `#version`,
// `local_size 8×8`, `image2D` and `vec2 size` push constant, which is precisely why CG was
// the one solver family that could not follow the solve bodies into 3D. Those declarations
// now come from the HOST — the same arrangement solve_jacobi / solve_rbgs have always had —
// and the cell math goes through ST_CELL / ST_OOB. Concatenate nd_2d and it is the old 2D
// kernel; concatenate nd_3d and it is the volume kernel.
//
// Host must supply, before this body: #version, local_size, the two r32f images (x_img @ set
// 2, y_img @ set 3), the Scalars SSBO @ set 5, and a push constant named `pc` whose FIRST
// member is the extent (vec2 in 2D, vec4 in 3D — the rule ST_SIZE already encodes) followed
// by `uint cy_slot; uint cx_slot;`.

void main() {
    ST_IVEC c = ST_CELL();
    if (ST_OOB(c)) {
        return;
    }
    float y = imageLoad(y_img, c).r;
    float x = imageLoad(x_img, c).r;
    imageStore(y_img, c, vec4(sc[pc.cy_slot] * y + sc[pc.cx_slot] * x, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
}
